\viewkind4\uc1\pard\cf1\ul\b\f0\fs24\'b6 Verse 1\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 1. Great God of wonders! all Thy ways
\par Display the attributes divine;
\par But countless acts of pardoning grace
\par Beyond Thine other wonders shine:
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Chorus\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par Who is a pardoning God like Thee?
\par Or who has grace so rich and free?
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 2\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 2. In wonder lost, with trembling joy
\par We taste the pardon of our God;
\par Pardon for crimes of deepest dye,
\par A pardon bought with Jesu's blood:
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Chorus\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par Who is a pardoning God like Thee?
\par Or who has grace so rich and free?
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 3\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 3. Pardon- from an offended God!
\par Pardon- for sins of deepest dye!
\par Pardon- bestowed through Jesu's blood!
\par Pardon- that brings the rebel nigh!
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Chorus\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par Who is a pardoning God like Thee?
\par Or who has grace so rich and free?
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 4\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 4. O may this strange, this matchless grace,
\par This God-like miracle of love,
\par Fill the wide earth with grateful praise,
\par As now it fills the choirs above!
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Chorus\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par Who is a pardoning God like Thee?
\par Or who has grace so rich and free?
\par \f1 
